1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,397
Stop hitting Enter on every Claude Code

2
00:00:02,454 --> 00:00:02,956
prompt.

3
00:00:03,089 --> 00:00:05,676
Shift+Tab twice gives you Plan mode.

4
00:00:06,126 --> 00:00:09,278
Default mode: Claude edits files immediately.

5
00:00:09,398 --> 00:00:12,156
Wrong dependency order, tests fail.

6
00:00:12,369 --> 00:00:14,955
In Plan mode, Claude proposes a plan

7
00:00:15,035 --> 00:00:15,595
first.

8
00:00:15,715 --> 00:00:17,828
You catch the order issue before any

9
00:00:17,892 --> 00:00:18,787
file is touched.

10
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:21,751
Shift+Tab twice cycles to Plan mode.

11
00:00:21,911 --> 00:00:24,233
Or use the slash-plan command.

12
00:00:24,347 --> 00:00:26,629
Claude writes a plan file — now

13
00:00:26,682 --> 00:00:27,906
named after your prompt.

14
00:00:28,046 --> 00:00:30,785
You read it, edit it, approve it.

15
00:00:31,393 --> 00:00:34,056
Best for refactors that touch multiple files,

16
00:00:34,136 --> 00:00:37,336
ambiguous prompts, or unfamiliar codebases.

17
00:00:37,423 --> 00:00:40,295
Production work where one wrong edit costs

18
00:00:40,375 --> 00:00:42,055
hours is the obvious case.

19
00:00:42,715 --> 00:00:43,655
Two keystrokes.

20
00:00:43,719 --> 00:00:44,935
That's the whole barrier.

21
00:00:45,063 --> 00:00:47,493
Most tutorials still skip Plan mode.

22
00:00:47,621 --> 00:00:50,138
Full series — link in description.
